1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,280
Six AI agents now do

2
00:00:01,300 --> 00:00:02,314
real work for you,

3
00:00:02,334 --> 00:00:03,489
even while you sleep.

4
00:00:04,203 --> 00:00:05,149
Same promise.

5
00:00:05,503 --> 00:00:06,752
Very different deals.

6
00:00:07,210 --> 00:00:08,049
Four of them live in a

7
00:00:08,069 --> 00:00:09,198
big company's cloud,

8
00:00:09,218 --> 00:00:10,455
on their own computer.

9
00:00:10,913 --> 00:00:12,379
Two are free, open source,

10
00:00:12,399 --> 00:00:13,497
and run on yours.

11
00:00:14,071 --> 00:00:16,074
First, OpenAI's Dots.

12
00:00:16,788 --> 00:00:18,660
Each dot gets its own cloud computer,

13
00:00:18,680 --> 00:00:20,506
links to over four thousand apps,

14
00:00:20,526 --> 00:00:22,285
and you can even text it on iMessage.

15
00:00:22,558 --> 00:00:24,108
It asks before it pays.

16
00:00:24,462 --> 00:00:26,311
It comes with ChatGPT Pro,

17
00:00:26,331 --> 00:00:27,611
from a hundred dollars a month,

18
00:00:27,631 --> 00:00:29,007
and it's not in Europe yet.

19
00:00:29,582 --> 00:00:31,443
Meta's Muse is the everyday helper.

20
00:00:31,463 --> 00:00:32,441
It books trips,

21
00:00:32,461 --> 00:00:34,357
shops, even negotiates your bills,

22
00:00:34,377 --> 00:00:35,637
right inside WhatsApp,

23
00:00:35,723 --> 00:00:37,494
and checks with you before it spends.

24
00:00:37,953 --> 00:00:39,082
Most tasks are free,

25
00:00:39,102 --> 00:00:40,861
with twenty and hundred dollar plans.

26
00:00:41,319 --> 00:00:42,646
For now, it's only in the

27
00:00:42,666 --> 00:00:43,903
US and Singapore.

28
00:00:44,256 --> 00:00:46,236
xAI's Grok Bot is the team player.

29
00:00:46,590 --> 00:00:48,184
Every bot gets its own computer,

30
00:00:48,204 --> 00:00:49,449
signs into your work apps,

31
00:00:49,469 --> 00:00:50,564
and joins your Slack,

32
00:00:50,584 --> 00:00:51,751
even your Zoom calls.

33
00:00:52,105 --> 00:00:53,443
It comes with X Premium at

34
00:00:53,463 --> 00:00:54,523
thirty dollars and up,

35
00:00:54,543 --> 00:00:56,186
and heavy use costs extra.

36
00:00:56,760 --> 00:00:57,901
Anthropic's Claude Duet

37
00:00:57,921 --> 00:00:58,984
is the careful one.

38
00:00:59,442 --> 00:01:00,595
It briefs you every morning,

39
00:01:00,615 --> 00:01:01,988
spots unpaid invoices,

40
00:01:02,008 --> 00:01:03,210
even runs payroll.

41
00:01:03,239 --> 00:01:04,159
Before it sends,

42
00:01:04,179 --> 00:01:05,903
pays, signs or deletes,

43
00:01:05,990 --> 00:01:07,085
it shows you and waits,

44
00:01:07,105 --> 00:01:07,967
and it never moves money

45
00:01:07,987 --> 00:01:09,038
between accounts.

46
00:01:09,392 --> 00:01:10,533
It's included in Claude Pro

47
00:01:10,553 --> 00:01:11,206
at twenty dollars,

48
00:01:11,226 --> 00:01:13,055
but it's a US waitlist preview.

49
00:01:13,409 --> 00:01:14,495
Now the free ones.

50
00:01:14,953 --> 00:01:16,245
OpenClaw, the lobster,

51
00:01:16,265 --> 00:01:17,336
has three hundred ninety-five

52
00:01:17,356 --> 00:01:18,640
thousand GitHub stars.

53
00:01:18,993 --> 00:01:20,390
It runs on your own computer,

54
00:01:20,410 --> 00:01:21,005
you chat with it on

55
00:01:21,025 --> 00:01:22,367
WhatsApp or Telegram,

56
00:01:22,395 --> 00:01:23,992
and the software costs nothing.

57
00:01:24,125 --> 00:01:24,941
But it can run commands

58
00:01:24,961 --> 00:01:25,463
on your machine,

59
00:01:25,483 --> 00:01:26,546
so lock it down.

60
00:01:27,260 --> 00:01:28,865
Hermes, from Nous Research,

61
00:01:28,885 --> 00:01:29,832
is the learner.

62
00:01:30,185 --> 00:01:31,129
After a hard task,

63
00:01:31,149 --> 00:01:32,220
it writes itself a new skill,

64
00:01:32,240 --> 00:01:33,988
so it gets better the more you use it.

65
00:01:34,261 --> 00:01:35,506
It's free with any AI model,

66
00:01:35,526 --> 00:01:37,343
or hosted from twenty dollars a month.

67
00:01:37,477 --> 00:01:38,954
The catch: you pick and set

68
00:01:38,974 --> 00:01:40,246
up the model yourself.

69
00:01:40,820 --> 00:01:41,697
So which one?

70
00:01:41,784 --> 00:01:43,090
Busy pro with budget:

71
00:01:43,444 --> 00:01:44,251
Dots.

72
00:01:44,280 --> 00:01:45,038
Everyday errands:

73
00:01:45,058 --> 00:01:45,758
Muse.

74
00:01:45,836 --> 00:01:47,445
A whole team: Grok Bot.

75
00:01:47,798 --> 00:01:49,743
Approval on every risky step:

76
00:01:50,016 --> 00:01:50,986
Claude Duet.

77
00:01:51,339 --> 00:01:52,724
Free and on your own machine:

78
00:01:52,744 --> 00:01:54,364
OpenClaw or Hermes.

79
00:01:54,637 --> 00:01:56,419
Save this before you pay for an agent.

80
00:01:56,773 --> 00:01:57,554
Which one would you trust

81
00:01:57,574 --> 00:01:58,590
with your inbox?

82
00:01:58,723 --> 00:01:59,786
Tell me below.
